  "limitations": [
    "Only null pointers or matching per-slot completed-helper requests establish readable direct-buffer extents; unknown non-null allocations are not read.",
    "Grown tails may contain arbitrary bytes. Captured zeros do not establish initialization. Only min(old,new) byte prefixes are classified for preservation.",
    "Per-slot tracking is scoped to this fixture; no populated object is destroyed/recreated and dimension is unchanged after allocation.",
    "Root tables can temporarily disagree with allocated containers. Root widths never determine reads of old allocations.",
    "Descriptor reads use storage begin/end bounds and retain raw bytes, including nonfinite floating-point values.",
    "No internal functions are invoked and no process memory is written. Only a fresh ready-gate file is written.",
    "Temporary boundary-builder chain ranges are not captured; persisted planar boundary nodes are captured."
  ],
